seg-7ab034787230 = EU NIS2 Directive, Article { "21" }: what Kshana supports evidence for

# text
seg-06480fd207dd = Article { "21" } lists, in paragraph { "2" } points (a) to (j), the measures essential and important entities take to manage risks to their network and information systems. Most points are organisational. Kshana speaks to the positioning-and-timing dependency of a system: how it behaves when GNSS is interfered with, and how that behaviour is tested and dated.

# text
# c1: kshana compliance-report
seg-ff0e00610721 = Every row says which Kshana outputs <b>support evidence for</b> the requirement and what is left over. Nothing here says a framework is met or that any product has been rated or approved by anyone. Run <c1/> on your own result files to see which rows your runs actually evidence; see <a1>README.md</a1>.

